      "displayName": "Genomic Location",
      "fullName": "GeneQuestions.GenesByLocation",
      "description": "Find genes that are located within a specified genomic region. Use either the Chromosome Tab or Sequence ID Tab \n         to define the genomic location you wish to query. The search returns all genes found \n         within your specified genomic location. <br><br>\n         \n         Chromosome Tab:<br>          \n         First select the Organism and Chromosome that you want to query. Then indicate the boundaries of \n         the genomic location by entering the Start and End nucleotide coordinates of your region. Choosing \n         Start=1 and End=0 will retrieve all genes on the chromosome.<br><br>\n         \n           \n         Sequence ID Tab:<br>\n         First enter the Genomic Sequence ID of the contig or chromosome that you \n         want to query. Example genomic sequence IDs are: Pf3D7_04_v3, AABL01000036, PviS_CM000452, berg12. Then indicate the boundaries of \n         the genomic location by entering the Start and End nucleotide coordinates of your region. Choosing \n         Start=1 and End=0 will retrieve all genes on the genomic sequence.<br>",
